## 4. Sequencing

### [LEC-SEQUENCE] Phased build + publish
- phase-1 (dispatched): STRUCTURAL CONSOLIDATION — [LEC-QUERY]+[LEC-ANALYTICS]+[LEC-LINT] as three defined layers + [LEC-RENAME] + [LEC-MOVES] + [LEC-AGENTIC-PROFILES] + [LEC-SPLIT]. On a clone of the clean staging factlattice.
- phase-2: [LEC-FRESHNESS] kernel — its own focused build on phase-1's result.
- phase-3 (architect): FINALIZE — ICPD removal + content-glass resolved + assemble the final library.
- phase-4 (architect): PUBLISH + DEPLOY — Plan A (delete-recreate the public repo) + stand up ~/factlattice-deployment (clean checkout + private overlay, gitignored) + ComposeIO re-point + MCP re-register (lts-engine) + console bounce. DONE 2026-07-23 (public repo @ 9d75bcd; re-point committed d414054, which also closed three LIVE breakages the rename left in the decision-ops WRITE path — hardcoded dead engine root, `MagmaStore`/`MagmaTools`, `magma_*` dispatch names).
- phase-5: [LEC-SELF-HEAL] — make stale a transient. Sequenced AFTER phase-2 because it consumes phase-2's maintained root as its "should I rebuild?" signal; without it phase-2 delivers a correct engine that goes dark on first write. DONE (unpushed) on branch `phase-3-self-heal` @ 9914369, 170 tests.
- outstanding-gates: NOTHING from phase 2 or 5 is live or public. `main` == `origin/main` == 9d75bcd; both builds sit on local branches. THREE deliberate gates remain, each David's call: (a) PUBLIC PUSH of phase-2 + phase-3 to github.com/740Dave/factlattice; (b) PROPAGATION — `~/factlattice-deployment` and the running `lts-engine` MCP server are still on phase-1 code, so the self-heal is not in effect for any live query; (c) a BOUNCE to pick up the ComposeIO re-point @ d414054 — the running decision-ops server predates it and its refresh-on-write currently fails with `ImportError: MagmaStore` (fail-safe: the write lands, only the refresh breaks).
- lifecycle-position: raised
- part-of: [SPEC:LTS-ENGINE-CONSOLIDATION]
